Z||000000||submitmls||10-01-2001||11:54 AM||||Hi guys. I need someone with edelbrock carb experience. I live at about 6,000 ft. I leaned out the carb according to spec by using<BR>.92 jets on the primaries and the rods that go with those specs. THe car runs leaner now but I have also lost power. If I go richer it won't pass emissions. I have no cats on my v8 set up. I will richen it up once the emissions thing is done but it wastes a lot of gas! I am wondering if any of you have a 650CFM edelbrok, live at about the same altitude and what combination jets and rods you've used to make your 350 run right. I have a 300hp factory rated 5.7L with a mild rv cam. I am afraid I won't pass emissions still even with the .92 jets on the primaries. ANy help would be appreciated.<BR>Oh, they say the problem is the car is running too rich, like 315 out of 183 maximumn CO's. Another question, how do you suggest they run the test on a v8 fiero when it was originally 4 cyl? What do I tell them?<BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
